pi.github.com/users/Flinterpop/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flinterpop/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":523060,"digest":"sha256:2242c661ad6804f217761f9072e7655eaaf25755d34a0d81dc2c83512b6b6879","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-07-28T21:03:04Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T21:03:04Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/Flinterpop/MDBoss/releases/download/v1.1.0/MDBoss-x86_64.AppImage.zsync"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Flinterpop/MDBoss/tarball/v1.1.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Flinterpop/MDBoss/zipball/v1.1.0","body":"First release carrying the **C++ port** alongside the Python app.\n\n### Both apps\n\n- **UTF-8 byte-order marks are handled.** A document saved by Notepad opened\n  with its first heading not being a heading, because the mark sat in front of\n  the `#`. Templates, `HELP.md` and imported favorites files were affected too\n  — the last of those failed to import at all, since JSON parsers reject a BOM.\n\n### MD Boss (C++) — new, Windows only\n\n`MDBoss-Cpp-Setup.exe` installs a C++/wxWidgets build of the same application,\nseparately from the Python one. About 5 MB, and it needs no VC++\nredistributable. The Python app remains the one that ships and the reference\nimplementation; the port is at feature parity but younger.\n\nIt reads and writes the **same** `%APPDATA%\\MDBoss\\config.json`, keeping its\nwindow layout under separate keys, so both builds can share one profile.\n\nTwo differences are deliberate:\n\n- It **reloads the open document when it changes on disk**, keeping your caret\n  and scroll position. Unsaved edits are never overwritten — they are kept and\n  the status bar says so. The Python app rescans on F5 only.\n- Code blocks are highlighted in the browser rather than server-side, so\n  colours in a fenced block differ slightly.\n\n`Help → Check for updates` points at the releases page rather than installing\nthe update itself; that path has not been exercised yet.\n\n### Notes\n\nThe preview stays network-locked in both builds: remote images, scripts and\nlinks inside a document are blocked, so document content never leaves your\nmachine.\n"}